<title>USA: Chemi-Trol to sell Cal-Van unit.</title>
<headline>Chemi-Trol to sell Cal-Van unit.</headline>
<dateline>GIBSONBURG, Ohio 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemi-Trol Chemical Co said it had signed a letter of intent to sell its Cal-Van Tools unit to Ronald A. Peterson Inc for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used by Chemi-Trol to retire debt, to invest in its core businesses or for other purposes, the company said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>Chemi-Trol, which makes steel pressure tanks for the storage of liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) and anhydrous ammonia, said that the move was part of a previously announced strategy to sell non-core businesses.</p>
<p>((-- David Chance, New York Newsroom 212 859-1902))</p>
